.TH DANBY-INTERNALCOMPETITION 1
.SH NAME
danby-internalcompetition \- predator-prey model with crowding in each species
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/internalcompetition
.SH MODEL
X' = X(a-bX-cY);
Y' = Y(eX-d-fY).
.PP
The terms bX and fY represent competition within the prey and predator
populations.  They replace the neutral family of Volterra orbits with bounded
density-dependent dynamics.  The positive nullcline intersection is marked.
.SH DISPLAY
The phase portrait shows approach to or departure from the coexistence point;
the time histories show damping, overshoot, and predator lag.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations.  The six bottom tracks set
birth, prey crowding, predation, conversion, death, and predator crowding.
Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/internalcompetition.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/internalcompetition.b
.SH SEE ALSO
